 "method": "Daily precipitation (pr, kg m-2 s-1 times 86400 = mm per day) at the grid cell over each field, summed April to June for every year. The dry-spring line is the 20th percentile of each model's own 1981-2014 springs. It catches 7 of those 34 springs in every model, which is 4.1 in 20; the 'baseline' of 4 is that rate in round numbers. Counts are springs at or below that line in 2040-2059. With no change, a line drawn from 34 springs catches about 4.3 of 20 future springs, not 4. Rain change is the 2040-2059 mean against the 1981-2014 mean. Median, lowest and highest are across models. 'chance_only' holds what the same number of models shows when rain does not change (200000 random draws, seed 20261114).",
 "chance_only": {
  "what": "What 8 models would show if spring rain did not change at all between 1981-2014 and 2040-2059.",
  "how": "200000 random draws with a fixed seed. Each draw gives every model 34 past and 20 future springs from one and the same rain distribution, draws the line the same way and counts the future springs at or below it. Springs are treated as independent from year to year and models as independent of each other. Ranges are 5th to 95th percentile.",
