 "caveats": [
  "Only one 0.25 degree grid square (about 28 by 19 km) around each sample farm was run. Fields elsewhere in the same county are outside that square, and the sample farm's numbers stand in for them.",
  "If rain did not change at all, 8 models would still usually show a middle value between about 2.5 and 6 dry springs in 20 years, a lowest model between 0 and 3 and a highest between 5 and 11 (each range holds at least 90 in 100 such cases). The line comes from only 34 past springs and is tested on only 20 future ones.",
  "The past rate is about 4 in 20. With no change a model shows about 4.3 in 20 on average, so a little over 4 is not a sign of change.",
  "One run per climate model. The chance ranges treat one spring as independent of the next.",
  "This is rain only. It does not cover heat, snow, or how a crop uses the rain.",
  "Each model is compared with its own 1981 to 2014 springs, not with rain gauges.",
  "Ritzville: model April to June rain (58 to 64 mm) runs below the NOAA rain gauge (77 mm, 1991 to 2020 normal, inside the same grid square). Use the counts, not the mm.",
  "Pullman: model April to June rain (108 to 118 mm) runs below the NOAA rain gauge (127 mm, 1991 to 2020 normal, 14 km from the field, outside the grid square). Use the counts, not the mm.",
  "Yearly rain totals were not read (only March to June days were downloaded), so there is no annual rain change here.",
  "12 models were planned and 8 are used. Not included: EC-Earth3, NorESM2-MM, CNRM-CM6-1, INM-CM5-0. They were not downloaded. They are the last ones in a fetch order that was fixed in fetch_future_rain.py."
 ],
